From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Subject: [PATCH] thermal/drivers/qcom/tsens-8960: Use the downstream sensor slopes

The downstream MSM8960/APQ8064 driver computes
  degC = 30 + (code - calib) * slope / 1000
with slope in milli-degC per ADC code. This driver computes
  degC = 30 + (code - p1) * 1000 / slope
with slope in codes per degC (x1000), but its table is the downstream
value minus 350, not its inverse. For the APQ8064 CPU sensors that is
-1.8% (sensors 7, 9: cpu0, cpu2) and +13% (sensors 8, 10: cpu1, cpu3) of
the distance from 30 C; cpu1 and cpu3 report 110 C at about 101 C.

Use 10^6 / downstream slope.

RISKY: also changes MSM8960 and IPQ8064 readings; unverified against a
reference thermometer.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
--- a/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens-8960.c
+++ b/drivers/thermal/qcom/tsens-8960.c
@@ -51,11 +51,17 @@
 #define S9_STATUS_OFF		0x3674
 #define S10_STATUS_OFF		0x3678
 
-/* Original slope - 350 to compensate mC to C inaccuracy */
+/*
+ * ADC codes per degree C, times 1000. The downstream driver specifies the
+ * inverse (milli-degC per code: 1176, 1176, 1154, 1176, 1111, 1132, 1132,
+ * 1199, 1132, 1199, 1132); these are 10^6 / those values. The previous
+ * "downstream - 350" values over-read sensors 4-6, 8 and 10 by 13-18% of
+ * the distance from the 30 C calibration point.
+ */
 static u32 tsens_msm8960_slope[] = {
-			826, 826, 804, 826,
-			761, 782, 782, 849,
-			782, 849, 782
+			850, 850, 867, 850,
+			900, 883, 883, 834,
+			883, 834, 883
 			};
 
 static int suspend_8960(struct tsens_priv *priv)
